# Committed TypeScript bindings generated by ts-proto from packages/protos - see the "Contract
# Layer" section of packages/protos/AGENTS.md for why committed rather than Pants-ephemeral, and
# packages/protos/buf.gen.yaml for the generator invocation. Regenerated by `buf generate` from
# packages/protos, checked for drift in CI (protos-drift in pull-request.yaml); never hand-edited.
#
# One recursive target for the whole tree rather than one per generated package: ts-proto writes a
# directory per proto package, and importing a well-known type pulls in its own
# (google/protobuf/timestamp.ts arrived with #169's Timestamp fields). A BUILD file per directory
# would mean a new unowned directory - and a `pants tailor --check` failure - every time a proto
# imports something new.
#
# The explicit dependency on packages/protos is what makes `pants dependents`/`--changed-since`
# resolve these bindings (and their Go counterparts) from a `.proto`-only edit - see #155. It's a
# plain BUILD-graph edge, not a codegen trigger: no TypeScript protobuf codegen backend is
# registered in pants.toml (there isn't one to enable), so nothing tries to generate TypeScript
# from this target.
typescript_sources(
    sources=["**/*.ts"],
    dependencies=["//packages/protos"],
)
